    verified:
      - "CORRECTNESS/REUSE/ALTITUDE/DESIGN, important — reported independently by FOUR finders. StepStatusView.remedy has exactly one render site (Onboarding.tsx:255-259, inside SetProxy), and TrustCa neither declares nor receives the prop. So three trustStatus remedies are computed, unit-tested, and dropped: notably 'install the certificate on the device you're capturing from'. This is a REGRESSION, not a gap — at b9e0bdb the screen rendered {view.glyph} {view.message} for every step, and that message WAS the full sentence including the instruction. The verifier grepped 'capturing from' repo-wide: it survives only in setup.ts (the data), two unit tests, and docs. No title/aria/alternate path surfaces it. The paired set-proxy test asserts getByTestId('set-proxy-remedy'); the absence of a trust-ca counterpart is why it slipped through."
      - "ALTITUDE, blocker — docs/use-cases/web-ui.html:205 (the T2 contract this WU itself updated) still states 'Traffic seen but not decrypting => the Trust step says \"install the certificate on the device you're capturing from\"'. After this diff that sentence renders nowhere. The doc asserts a capability the running code lost, which is the worst class of doc defect: it was edited in this WU and left describing the old behaviour."
      - "CORRECTNESS/REUSE, important — Onboarding.tsx:267-274 renders the proxy command TWICE for all four snippet targets. proxySteps(target, addr) (setup.ts:151,153,155,163) already splices `snippet!` into its array, and SetProxy appends proxySnippet(target, addr) again as a CopyText. Verified by rendering the real component: macOS shows step 2 and step 3 byte-identical. Linux is worse — the duplicate is non-adjacent (command, unrelated sentence, same command). A regression: at base the snippet lived in a separate button OUTSIDE the <ol>. ProxyCloseDialog.tsx:134-141 solves the same problem correctly by REPLACING the trailing step. Tests missed it because they assert toHaveTextContent(/networksetup/), a substring regex that passes at any multiplicity."
      - "DESIGN, important — Checkbox.tsx:17 declares @states 'hover and focus (the border lifts to ink-mute, one channel)', but the input carries only `accent-ink-mute outline-none`: no border, no hover:, no focus: class, and outline-none removes the native ring. Verifier grepped index.css, tailwind.config.js (plugins: []), and index.html — nothing restores it, and no focus-within/has-[:focus] exists anywhere. accent-color tints the check, not the focus. Every other focusable registry member carries focus-visible:outline, and collection.test.tsx:158 asserts it for the Button family; Checkbox escapes only because it is not a <button>. A WCAG 2.4.7 failure on a control shipped inside a modal, plus a false @states contract in a registry whose TSDoc is normative."
      - "SIMPLIFICATION/ALTITUDE, important — ProxyCloseDialog.test.tsx:187 'traps Tab inside the panel' verifies nothing. PROVEN BY MUTATION: the verifier deleted the entire Tab branch from ModalShell's trap and the file still passed 28/28. jsdom does not move focus on keyDown, so the assertion (focus is inside the dialog) is already true before the event dispatches. The trap is entirely untested; grep for 'Tab' across all test files finds only this and an unrelated Select case."
