      - "SIMPLIFICATION/ALTITUDE, important — StepStatusView.message now has ZERO production consumers. StatusLine renders .short; no other component or screen reads .message (the one grep hit, StatusPill.tsx:15, is an unrelated statuses.message lookup table). All 16 resolver branches still build the full sentence, pinned by a test asserting it. Either the field earns a stated reason to exist or it goes."
      - "SIMPLIFICATION, important — onboardingMachine.ts:16-17,37-39: the `next`/`back` events and the shift() helper that serves only them are dead after this diff removed the Back/Next buttons. Nothing in production dispatches either (verified by grep excluding tests); the tests now assert the buttons must NOT exist. Two reduce() branches kept alive solely by their own unit test."
